  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a binary star system of star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> with masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> revolving in a circular orbit of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> are the time period of star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively, then:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub></math>&nbsp;(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub></math>)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>1) From the centre of mass, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>2) Force acting&nbsp;on both starts i.e. gravitational force and centripetal force are balanced.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>GM</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>As we know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#38;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Substituting equation 3 in equation 2, we get&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>From equation 1, we conclude in eqution 4</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
